   166	The heading's “two components” can only mean the two source dicriticals.
   167	Under H2 there is one target component, so the repaired \(N=4\)
   168	two-target aggregate must not be copied componentwise.  The exact analogue
   169	of its \(s_0=1,c_0=1\) repair is
   170	
   171	\[
   172	 s_2=s_1=1,\qquad l_2'\simeq l_1'\simeq\widetilde D\simeq\mathbf A^1,
   173	 \qquad c=1.                                                          \tag{3.1}
   174	\]
   175	
   176	Indeed, Orevkov Lemma 2.1 gives \(l_i'\simeq\mathbf A^1\), and either
   177	degree-one finite map \(h_i\) in (2.1) identifies it with the one common
   178	normalization.  This is the same primary-source affine-line repair used
   179	in review 321--337, now applied to the promoted degrees (1.1).
   180	
   181	The promoted irreducible Euler calculation (proof 236--265, with the
   182	equality repair at review 181--212) is
   183	
   184	\[
   185	 \chi_c(D-\Sigma)=2-c-\nu-\sigma,
   186	 \qquad
   187	 (N-a)\chi_c(D-\Sigma)=N-1-N\sigma+A.                                \tag{3.2}
   188	\]
   189	
   190	Putting \((N,a)=(5,2)\) gives
   191	
   192	\[
   193	 3c+3\nu-2\sigma+A=2.                                                 \tag{3.3}
   194	\]
   195	
   196	With (3.1), this becomes the exact \(N=5\) aggregate
   197	
   198	\[
   199	 3\nu+A=2\sigma-1.                                                    \tag{3.4}
   200	\]
   201	
   202	### 3.1 Pointwise fibre equation and the correction contribution
   203	
   204	Let \(p_*=\phi_2(x)\), and put \(\iota_p=1\) for \(p=p_*\), zero
   205	otherwise.  Let \(B_i\) denote the finite-model boundary prime
   206	corresponding to \(l_i\).  Local degree is additive over branches
   207	specializing to one physical fibre point.  Hence two distinct
   208	normalization places of \(B_1\) could coalesce only with local
   209	multiplicity at least two, contradicting
   210	\(\operatorname{corr}_1=0\); two places of \(B_2\) would give at least
   211	four, contradicting its total correction one.  A cross-dicritical
   212	collision would give at least \(1+2=3\), and in particular a positive
   213	correction on \(B_1\).  Thus all these physical points are distinct.
   214	For every normalization place over \(p\), \(l_1'\) therefore supplies one
   215	boundary point of local multiplicity one and \(l_2'\) one of local
   216	multiplicity two, except that the marked \(l_2'\)-point has multiplicity
   217	three.  There are no separate \(L_C\) “epsilon” points in the repaired
   218	finite model; the contrary term in the printed \(N=4\) identity was
   219	refuted (integration 56--66, 108--111; review 308--337).
