+\]
+
+Both target normalizations are \(\mathbb A^1\). The nontrivial component \(D_1\) is a singular polynomial curve whose affine singularities are double points of two smooth branches, disjoint from the trivial component. Its complement must surject onto \(S_4\), with all meridians transpositions and the two local meridians at every double point disjoint. This is exactly OPEN[PI1-S4] at **Coord:84--106**; a negative answer closes B0 at \(N=4\) without H2.
+
+There is no promoted single PI1-\(S_N\) analogue for \(N\ge5\). The honest remainder is:
